# Canonical identity for the contributor graph.
#
# One person, recorded under four spellings over time: the GitHub handle, the
# full name, a typo of the handle, and the commits that had been attributed to an
# assistant as author rather than co-author.
#
# The canonical address is the GitHub noreply form. A personal address in commit
# metadata becomes public the moment a repository does, and a mailmap does not
# hide it, so the history itself was rewritten on 2026-10-07 to use noreply
# throughout. This file collapses the remaining name variants.
#
# Assistance is recorded where it belongs: in the Co-Authored-By trailer of the
# commits it applies to, never in the author field.
